<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<lint>
    <!--
      The legacy round launcher bitmaps intentionally share the same artwork as the standard icon.
      API 26+ applies the launcher mask to the adaptive icon, and minSdk is 26; keeping the aliases
      still accommodates launchers that consult android:roundIcon.
    -->
    <issue id="IconDuplicates">
        <ignore regexp="mipmap-.*/ic_launcher_round\.webp" />
    </issue>

    <!--
      Room's generated `_Impl` classes call `@RestrictTo(LIBRARY_GROUP)` types — `EntityUpsertAdapter`
      and friends — which is how Room is built: the generated code is meant to be part of the library
      group and the check has no way to know that. Nobody here can change a line of it.

      It only became visible in step A6, when the `@Database` class moved to `:shared`. AGP marks the
      KSP output of the project being linted as generated and skips it; the lint model a Kotlin
      Multiplatform module contributes to `checkDependencies` does not, so the same generated code
      that was invisible in `:app` is read as ordinary source in `:shared`. Scoped by path so that a
      `@RestrictTo` violation in code somebody actually wrote still fails the build.
    -->
    <issue id="RestrictedApi">
        <ignore regexp="build/generated/ksp/" />
    </issue>
</lint>
